<!-- Binaries linked against the macOS 26+ SDK adopt Liquid Glass rendering,
     under which the NSVisualEffectView material gpui uses for blurred window
     backgrounds no longer frosts behind-window content. This key opts back
     into the pre-Liquid-Glass design. Official Zed builds link an older SDK
     and are unaffected; local builds use the installed Xcode SDK. Caveat:
     Apple documents the key as ignored when building with the macOS 27+ SDK,
     so under current Xcode-beta it may be inert - it is kept as zero-risk
     compatibility for 26.x-SDK builds, and the lasting fix is a gpui blur
     material that still frosts under Liquid Glass. -->
<key>UIDesignRequiresCompatibility</key>
<true/>
